## Villa, Terrace, Beach Club or Garden

Every outdoor venue has its own constraints. A villa or private garden usually has its own power point but variable ground surface for cable runs. A hotel terrace or beach club often has house power confirmed in advance through the venue. A rooftop adds wind exposure that affects where we place lighting stands and speakers.

Our [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) suits a smaller outdoor party, up to 50 guests, delivered and set up by our crew, self-run with no technician included. Our [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) suits a larger outdoor wedding or celebration, up to 80 guests, with a technician included on site and fairy lights for evening ambiance.

<InlineCTA />

## Power and Weather, Honestly

We do not rent generators or tents. Confirm your venue's power access when you book, and we will size the sound and lighting setup to match what is actually available. For weather, our technicians assess conditions on site and plan equipment placement around whatever shelter the venue provides; if rain is a real risk, arrange a covered backup area with your venue in advance.

Sound also behaves differently outdoors: with no walls to reflect off, open air disperses sound further, so our PA systems are set up to project across the space rather than fill a room.

