## FAQs

### What happens to AV equipment if it rains during an outdoor event?

We do not rent tents or canopies, so if rain is a real risk, arrange a covered backup area with your venue in advance. Our technicians assess conditions on site and place equipment around whatever shelter is available.

### Do you provide a generator for venues without power access?

No, generators are not part of our catalog. Confirm your venue's power access with us when you book, and we will size the sound and lighting setup to match what is actually available.

### How does an outdoor sound system differ from an indoor one?

With no walls to reflect sound, open air disperses audio further than an indoor room does. Our PA systems are set up to project across the outdoor space rather than fill a closed room.

### Is a technician included for an outdoor event?

It depends on the package. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then self-run, no technician included. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes a technician on site.

### What outdoor venues do you set up at?

We set up at villas, private gardens, hotel terraces, beach clubs and rooftops across Malaga and the wider Costa del Sol, extending to Granada for rentals over 400 euros.

### Can lighting and sound equipment run on grass, sand or uneven ground?

Yes, our crew manages cable runs and stand placement for the actual ground surface at your venue when we install the equipment.

### How far in advance should I book AV equipment for an outdoor event?

Book at least 24 hours in advance to guarantee availability. For a larger outdoor event with weather to plan around, book as early as you can once your date and venue are confirmed.
